RULES = {
    "CrossingEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid Crossing (also called LavaCrossing or SimpleCrossing). The room is cut by one or more straight barriers — each barrier is a full row or column of either lava or wall — and every barrier has exactly one safe one-cell opening. You start in the top-left and the green goal sits in the bottom-right.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Stepping into a lava tile ends the episode in failure — only move forward when the cell ahead is plain floor or the goal.\n- Each barrier has only **one** gap, and it can be anywhere along the line. Locate it by looking before you commit to forward movement; rotating in place is always safe.\n- The level has no objects to pick up — pickup, drop, and toggle have no effect.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "PutNearEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid PutNear. A single room holds a few objects — keys, balls and boxes of different colors, placed far apart from each other. The mission names one object to move and one object to move it next to. You must carry the first object over and put it down in a cell adjacent to the second.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or through a cell occupied by an object. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- `pickup` only works when the object is in the cell **directly in front of you** and your hands are empty.\n- DANGER: picking up the **wrong** object immediately ends the episode with **0 reward**. Match both the color word and the object type in the mission before you press `pickup`.\n- DANGER: `drop` ends the episode **no matter where you drop**. You get the reward only if the object lands in one of the 8 cells surrounding the target object (diagonals count); anywhere else scores 0. You get exactly one placement attempt.\n- `drop` puts the carried object into the empty cell directly in front of you. If that cell is not empty the drop fails and the episode does not end — but you have wasted a step, so line yourself up carefully first.\n- The intended sequence is: walk to the object named first, face it, `pickup`, walk until you are standing next to the target object, turn so that an **empty cell adjacent to the target** is directly in front of you, then `drop`.\n- This evaluation allows at most 30 environment actions. Do not spend turns scanning — plan your route from the screenshot and move.\n- You never need `toggle` or `done` here; both only waste steps.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n- drop: Put down what you are carrying into the empty cell directly in front of you.\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.",
    "DynamicObstaclesEnv": '# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid DynamicObstacles. The room is otherwise empty, but several blue balls drift around the floor and reposition themselves every step. The green goal sits in the corner, and bumping into one of these moving balls ends the run.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- Moving forward into a wall or a non-goal occupied cell ends the episode with a -1 reward.\n- The obstacles move every single step — predict where they could land next, not just where they are right now.\n- Walking forward into an obstacle (or any non-goal cell that is occupied) ends the episode immediately with a -1 penalty.\n- Turning in place is a safe way to wait out a dangerous neighbor; use it as a "stall" action when the path ahead is unsafe.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.',
    "UnlockEnv1": '# Game\nYou are playing a Minigrid/BabyAI Unlock level. The level contains one or more **locked** doors, and for each of them a key of the same color lies somewhere in the rooms. Read the mission to see what finishes the episode: usually it is opening a named door, but in some variants the goal is to pick up an object that is shut away behind locked doors.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or through a door that is closed or locked. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- `pickup` only works when the object is in the cell **directly in front of you** and **your hands are empty**. Move next to it and face it first.\n- `toggle` on a locked door only unlocks it while you are **carrying a key of the same color** as that door, standing directly in front of it. Toggling it empty-handed, or holding a wrong-color key, does nothing.\n- Unlocked doors in the way are simply closed: `toggle` in front of one opens it with no key needed.\n- Because you can only hold one thing at a time, `drop` the key you no longer need before picking up something else. Dropping puts the carried object into the empty cell directly in front of you, and fails silently if that cell is occupied.\n- Some variants chain the locks: the key for door A is behind door B, so you must unlock B first, fetch A\'s key, and then unlock A.\n- Opening a door that the mission did not ask for does not end the episode and does not lose points — it just costs steps.\n- If the mission says "open the ... door", the episode ends with a reward the moment that door becomes open. If it says "pick up the ...", it ends the moment you pick that object up. You do not need `done`; issuing it just wastes a step.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n- drop: Put down what you are carrying into the empty cell directly in front of you.\n- toggle: Open the door in the cell directly in front of you (a locked door also needs the matching key in hand).\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.',
    "UnlockPickupEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing a MiniGrid/BabyAI UnlockPickup. There are two rooms joined by a single **locked** door. You start in the left room together with a key that matches the door's color; the box named in the mission is in the right room. You must take the key, unlock the door, go through, put the key down, and pick up the box.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or through a door that is closed or locked. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- `pickup` only works when the object is in the cell **directly in front of you** and **your hands are empty**. Move next to it and face it first.\n- `toggle` on the locked door only unlocks it while you are **carrying the matching key**, standing directly in front of it. Toggling it empty-handed does nothing.\n- This is the trap of this level: after unlocking the door you are still holding the key, so `pickup` on the box would silently fail. You must `drop` the key first, then face the box and `pickup`.\n- `drop` places what you carry into the empty cell directly in front of you. It fails silently if that cell is occupied, so face an empty floor cell before dropping. Do not drop the key inside the doorway.\n- The episode ends with a reward the moment you `pickup` the box named in the mission. You do not need `done`; issuing it just wastes a step.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n- drop: Put down what you are carrying into the empty cell directly in front of you.\n- toggle: Unlock/open the door in the cell directly in front of you (needs the matching key in hand).\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.",
    "LavaGapEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid LavaGap. The room is split in two by a single vertical strip of lava that has exactly one safe gap somewhere along it. You start on one side and the green goal is on the other.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Stepping into a lava tile ends the episode in failure — never move forward into a lava cell.\n- The gap is exactly one tile of plain floor inside the lava strip; locate it before crossing instead of guessing.\n- The level has no objects to pick up — pickup, drop, and toggle have no effect.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "BabyAI-GoToDoor": "# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToDoor. The level is a single room with up to four colored doors set into its walls — one per side. The mission picks a door by color, and your job is just to stand next to it.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or closed doors. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the correct-color door from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`, and you do not need to toggle the door open.\n- All four doors look the same except for color, so identify the right one by reading the mission's color word carefully.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "DistShiftEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid DistShift. The room is a small corridor with two horizontal strips of lava running across it. You start in the top-left corner and the green goal sits in the top-right corner. The exact row of the second lava strip can vary between episodes — that is the whole point of this level, so don't rely on a memorized path.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Stepping into a lava tile ends the episode in failure — only move forward when the cell ahead is plain floor or the goal.\n- Re-check the lava layout in every episode; the configuration may not match what you have seen before.\n- The level has no objects to pick up — pickup, drop, and toggle have no effect.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "BlockedUnlockPickupEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing a MiniGrid/BabyAI BlockedUnlockPickup. Two rooms are joined by a single **locked** door, and a ball is sitting in the cell right in front of that door, blocking the way. You start in the left room with the matching key; the box named in the mission is in the right room. You must clear the ball out of the doorway, unlock the door, put the key down, and pick up the box.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls, through a door that is closed or locked, or through a cell occupied by a ball or box. Bumping into any of them does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- You can carry only **one** thing at a time. `pickup` only works when the object is in the cell **directly in front of you** and **your hands are empty**.\n- The ball in front of the door cannot be pushed. You must `pickup` the ball, turn to face a free floor cell, and `drop` it somewhere out of the way before you can reach the door.\n- `drop` places what you carry into the empty cell directly in front of you. It fails silently if that cell is occupied, so face an empty floor cell before dropping.\n- `toggle` on the locked door only unlocks it while you are **carrying the matching key**, standing directly in front of it. Toggling it empty-handed does nothing — and since you can only hold one item, you cannot be carrying both the ball and the key.\n- After unlocking you are still holding the key, so `pickup` on the box would silently fail. `drop` the key first, then face the box and `pickup`.\n- The whole level therefore needs `pickup`/`drop` three times over: move the ball, take the key, put the key down.\n- The episode ends with a reward the moment you `pickup` the box named in the mission. You do not need `done`; issuing it just wastes a step.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n- drop: Put down what you are carrying into the empty cell directly in front of you.\n- toggle: Unlock/open the door in the cell directly in front of you (needs the matching key in hand).\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.",
    "BabyAI-GoTo": '# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoTo. The map is a multi-room maze (a 3x3 grid of rooms by default) connected by colored doors, with many distractor objects scattered across the rooms. The target object named in the mission may be in your starting room or somewhere on the other side of the maze.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or closed doors. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the correct object from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- Doors between rooms may start closed; use `toggle` (action 5) on a door you are facing to open it, then walk through.\n- If the mission uses the article "a" (e.g. "go to a green box"), any object that matches the description is acceptable; with "the", you should head for the unique matching object.\n- Distractors share types and colors with the target; only the (color, type) pair uniquely identifies it, so always check both.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- toggle: Interact with the object in front (open/close door).',
    "GoToObjectEnv": '# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid GoToObject. A single room contains a small handful of objects — keys, balls, and boxes in various colors — and the mission picks one of them as the target. Your job is just to walk up to it.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- The mission identifies the target by both color AND type (e.g. "the red ball" is different from "the red key" or "the blue ball"). Match both.\n- Success requires being **orthogonally adjacent** to the correct object (any of its four neighbor cells) AND issuing `done`. You do **not** need to face it.\n- WARNING: pressing `toggle` (action 5) at any point immediately ends the episode with **0 reward**. Never toggle in this level.\n- Issuing `done` while you are not next to the target also ends the episode with 0 reward, so confirm your position before pressing it.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- done: Signal task completion.',
    "RedBlueDoorEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid RedBlueDoors. You start inside a room that has exactly two doors: a red one in the left wall and a blue one in the right wall. Neither is locked. Your task is to open them **in order**: the red door first, then the blue one.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through a closed door. `toggle` in front of a door opens it; no key is needed anywhere in this level.\n- The order is the whole puzzle, and getting it wrong is fatal:\n  - Opening the **blue** door while the red one is still closed ends the episode immediately with **0 reward**.\n  - Opening the red door first and the blue door afterwards ends the episode with the reward.\n- So the only winning sequence is: reach the red door, `toggle` it, then cross to the blue door and `toggle` it. Do not touch the blue door before the red one is open.\n- `toggle` also **closes** a door that is already open. If you toggle the red door twice it becomes closed again and opening the blue door will then score 0, so leave the red door open and walk away.\n- The two doors are on opposite walls, so expect to cross the room between the two toggles.\n- You never need `pickup`, `drop` or `done` here; they only waste steps.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- toggle: Open the door in the cell directly in front of you.\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.",
    "FourRoomsEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid FourRooms. The map is split into four rooms by a cross of inner walls. Adjacent rooms are connected by a single one-cell opening (no doors), and both your starting position and the green goal are placed at random anywhere across the four rooms.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- There are no doors here — the only way between rooms is through the open gaps in the inner walls, so plan your path room-to-room and aim for the gap on the side facing your destination.\n- The level has no lava and no objects to pick up — pickup, drop, and toggle have no effect.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "BabyAI-GoToLocal": "# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToLocal. The level is a single room with several objects scattered around. The mission names one of them, and several distractors share the same type or color so you have to read carefully.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the correct object from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- Distractors can match either the color or the type alone; only the (color, type) pair uniquely identifies the target, so always check both.\n- You do not need to pick anything up — pickup, drop, and toggle are not required to solve this level.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "DoorKeyEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid DoorKey. A vertical wall splits the room in two, with a single yellow locked door in it. You start on the left side together with a yellow key; the green goal square sits in the bottom-right corner on the far side. You must pick up the key, unlock the door, walk through, and step onto the goal.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or through a door that is closed or locked. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- `pickup` only works when the key is in the cell **directly in front of you** and your hands are empty. Move next to the key and face it first.\n- `toggle` on the locked door only unlocks it while you are **carrying the yellow key** and standing directly in front of the door. Toggling it empty-handed does nothing.\n- Once the door is open you can walk straight through it. Keep carrying the key — you never need to drop it in this level.\n- The episode ends with a reward the moment you step **onto** the green goal cell. You do not need `done`; issuing it just wastes a step.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n- toggle: Unlock/open the door in the cell directly in front of you (needs the matching key in hand).\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.",
    "FetchEnv": '# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid Fetch. A single open room contains several keys and balls in assorted colors. The mission names exactly one of them. You must walk up to that object and pick it up — and nothing else.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- The mission is phrased loosely ("get a", "go get a", "fetch a", "go fetch a", "you must fetch a"), but the part that matters is the **color** and the **object type** at the end of the sentence.\n- You cannot walk through walls or through a cell occupied by an object. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- `pickup` only works when the object is in the cell **directly in front of you** and your hands are empty.\n- DANGER: this level ends the instant you are holding **anything**. Picking up the correct object wins; picking up **any** other object immediately ends the episode with **0 reward**. There is no second chance and no way to undo it by dropping.\n- So never press `pickup` unless the object directly in front of you matches both the color and the type named in the mission. When in doubt, turn or step to get a clearer look rather than risking the pickup.\n- Keys and balls of the same color look different: a key has a stem and a round head, a ball is a plain filled circle. Check the shape as well as the color.\n- You never need `drop`, `toggle` or `done` here; they only waste steps.\n- Faster is better: the reward is `1 - 0.9 * (step_count / native_max_steps)`, so every wasted turn lowers your score. Running out of steps scores 0.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- pickup: Pick up the object in the cell directly in front of you (only if your hands are empty).\n\nThere are no other actions. In particular there is no `up`, `down`, `north` or `south`: to move in a different direction you must `left`/`right` until you face it, then `forward`.',
    "BabyAI-GoToRedBallGrey": '# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToRedBallGrey. The level is a single room with one red ball and several distractor objects, but every distractor is forced to be grey — so the red ball is the only colored thing in the room.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the red ball from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- The grey distractors are intentionally drained of color cues, so simply heading toward "the red thing" is a reliable strategy.\n- You do not need to pick anything up — pickup, drop, and toggle are not required to solve this level.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.',
    "EmptyEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid Empty. The level is a single rectangular room enclosed by walls, with nothing inside it except a green goal square in the far corner. There are no hazards, no doors, and no objects to pick up.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- This level contains no lava, no doors, and no objects — pickup, drop, and toggle have no effect here.\n- The shortest solution is purely navigation: orient yourself, then walk straight toward the goal.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "BabyAI-GoToRedBlueBall": "# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToRedBlueBall. The level is a single room with exactly one red ball, one blue ball, and a handful of distractors that are guaranteed to be neither red nor blue balls. The mission picks one of the two balls as the target.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the correct ball from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- The room contains exactly **one** red ball and **one** blue ball; distractors will never be red or blue balls, so the target is always unambiguous.\n- You do not need to pick anything up — pickup, drop, and toggle are not required to solve this level.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "BabyAI-GoToRedBall": "# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToRedBall. The level is a single room with one red ball and a number of colored distractor objects. The mission is always the same: go to the red ball.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the red ball from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- Distractors come in many colors and types but the room is guaranteed to contain only **one** red ball, so it is unambiguous which one is the target.\n- You do not need to pick anything up — pickup, drop, and toggle are not required to solve this level.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
    "GoToDoorEnv": "# Game\nYou are playing Minigrid GoToDoor. A single room has up to four colored doors, one on each wall. The mission tells you which color to walk up to — your job is to stand next to that door and signal completion. You do not need to open any door.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls or closed doors. Bumping into either does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success requires being **orthogonally adjacent** to the correct-color door (any of its four neighbor cells) AND issuing `done`. You do **not** need to face it.\n- WARNING: pressing `toggle` (action 5) at any point — even on the right door — immediately ends the episode with **0 reward**. Never toggle in this level.\n- Issuing `done` while you are not next to the target door also ends the episode with 0 reward, so confirm your position before pressing it.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.\n- done: Signal task completion.",
    "BabyAI-GoToObj": '# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToObj. The level is a single room that contains exactly one object — and that one object is your target. The mission tells you its color and type, e.g. "go to the red ball".\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the target object from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- Object types are one of {ball, box, key} and colors are one of {red, green, blue, purple, yellow, grey}.\n- Since there is only one object in the whole room, you cannot mistake the target for a distractor.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.',
    "BabyAI-GoToRedBallNoDists": "# Game\nYou are playing BabyAI GoToRedBallNoDists. The level is a single room with exactly one object — a red ball — and nothing else to confuse you. The mission is always the same: go to the red ball.\n\n## Objective\n- Follow the Mission in the current observation.\n\n## Rules\n- You cannot walk through walls. Bumping into a wall does nothing and just wastes the action.\n- Success is checked automatically: as soon as you are facing the red ball from the adjacent cell, the episode ends with a reward — you do not need to press `done`.\n- There are no distractors in this level — anything you spot in the room that is not a wall is the target.\n\n# Action Space\nChoose exactly one action per step:\n- left: Turn 90 degrees left in place (does not move).\n- right: Turn 90 degrees right in place (does not move).\n- forward: Move one cell forward in the direction you are facing.",
}
